---
layout: base.njk
pagination:
  data: curriculum.tracks
  alias: track
  size: 1
permalink: "genres/{{ track.slug }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ track.title }} Drum Lessons"
  description: "{{ track.description }}"
---

<div class="lesson-layout">

{% set currentTrack = track.slug %}
{% include "section-nav.njk" %}

<div class="container">
  {#- Title block, system.md §8.3. The breadcrumb is the real component now —
      the hand-rolled inline-styled copy that used to sit here was the last
      inline style on the page (BL-032). It also says "Genres", which is what
      the old `Genre Path` eyebrow said one line above it, so the eyebrow is
      deleted rather than restyled (same call as §6.1 on lesson pages).
      The tagline moves out of the h1: a title and its slogan are two thoughts
      and only the title is the page's name. -#}
  <header class="genre-hero">
    <p class="breadcrumb">
      {#- &nbsp; after each separator: see the note in lessons.njk (BL-044). -#}
      <a href="/">Lessons</a>
      <span class="breadcrumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>&nbsp;<a href="/#tracks">Genres</a>
      <span class="breadcrumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>&nbsp;{{ track.title }}
    </p>
    <h1>{{ track.title }}</h1>
    <p class="lede">{{ track.tagline }}</p>
    <p class="genre-hero__desc">{{ track.description }}</p>
  </header>

  {#- Level blocks are ledger sections (§8.3): the head keeps its .level-block
      classes and the lists are the homepage's ledger rows, reused rather than
      forked, so a lesson looks the same wherever the town lists it. Numbering
      restarts per block, exactly as it does per chapter on the homepage.
      No state mark here — the ✓/●/○ vocabulary is only legible next to the
      legend that defines it, which lives on the homepage. -#}
  {% for level in track.levels %}
  <section class="level-block">
    <header class="level-block__header">
      <h2 class="level-block__title">{{ level.title }}</h2>
      <span class="level-block__tag">{{ level.lessons.length }} lessons</span>
    </header>

    <ol class="ledger__rows">
      {% for lesson in level.lessons %}
        <li><a class="ledger-row" href="/lessons/{{ lesson.slug }}/">
          <span class="ledger-row__num">{{ loop.index | pad2 }}</span>
          <span class="ledger-row__title">{{ lesson.title }}</span>
          <span class="ledger-row__leader" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="ledger-row__meta"><span class="ledger-row__min">{{ lessonContent[lesson.slug].duration }}</span></span>
        </a></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

</div>{# /.lesson-layout #}
